use a PostgreSQL DB to replace a Windows/IIS/SQL Server stack:
step 1: pull the postgres image and run
$ podman pull docker.io/library/postgres:17 --tls-verify=false                 //have to use postgres 17 for now
$ podman inspect docker.io/library/postgres                                    //to get the ExposedPorts (here 5432)
$ podman run --% -d --name my-postgres -p 1234:5432 -v pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=password docker.io/library/postgres:17     
                                                                               //host port:container port, host port value can be 1024-65535
$ podman ps                                                                    //verify
note: 
copy ouput contents ctrl+shift+C
remove a container: $ podman rm -f <container-name>



step 2: spin up the container
step 3: expose network ports
step 4: migrate schema and data
step 5: update connection strings

